  "html": "<section class=\"container section--services-hero pt-5\">\n\t<div class=\"section--services-hero__main\">\n\t\t<div class=\"section--services-hero__main__row\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"section--services-hero__main__row__left\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group flow has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group h-align icon-plus-title is-layout-flex wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">    <div class=\"iconblock wp-elements-1 has-background has-secondary-background-color has-text-color has-secondary-inverse-color\" data-size=\"md\" data-padding=\"2\" data-display=\"inline\">\n        <svg class=\"icon\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-hvac\" /></svg>    </div>\n\n<h1 class=\"has-link-color wp-elements-2 wp-block-post-title has-text-color has-secondary-color has-x-large-font-size\">Gas Pack Services in Greenville, SC</h1></div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group services-hero-description flow is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<p>Gas pack installation, repair, and maintenance for homes throughout Greenville, SC.</p>\n<p>If your home runs on a gas pack, Carolina Heating Service installs, repairs, and maintains packaged units throughout Greenville, SC and the Upstate. Certified technicians work on both the gas heating side and the electric cooling side of the unit, which matters because a gas pack puts both systems in one cabinet.</p>\n<p>Gas packs are common in homes without a basement, attic, or closet space for indoor equipment, since the entire system sits outside on a pad or a rooftop. That design also means every component lives outdoors year-round, so weather exposure makes regular maintenance a bigger factor in equipment life than it is for split systems.</p>\n\n</div>\n\n<div  class=\"wp-block-group mb-3 full-width-mobile schedule-and-call-cta is-content-justification-left is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-a1b15d37 wp-block-